      "headline": {
        "en": "Lenders take control as French restructurings rise",
        "zh": "法国重组增加，贷款人接管企业"
      },
      "summary": {
        "en": "Debtwire data shows France recorded 39 restructuring mandates in the first half of 2026, covering €14.57bn of debt. Lenders including CVC Credit, KKR, Blackstone and HIG Capital took elderly care operator Colisée from EQT, cutting net debt by about a third to €1.2bn and adding €285m of new financing; bondholders also took ownership of Atalian in June.",
        "zh": "Debtwire数据显示，法国在2026年上半年录得39宗重组委托，涉及145.7亿欧元债务。包括CVC Credit、KKR、Blackstone和HIG Capital在内的贷款人从EQT手中接管养老护理运营商Colisée，将其净债务削减约三分之一至12亿欧元，并注入2.85亿欧元新融资；6月债券持有人还接管了Atalian。"
      },
